From 222a3f26701b6fb05bf78f938ce60abf611c964a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: yinvoker <yinvoker@outlook.com>
Date: Tue, 1 Sep 2026 11:31:58 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] perf: persistent ruy contexts + prepacked cache for constant
 weights

- one thread_local ruy::Context per worker thread instead of one per GEMM
  call (int8 and float paths); restores ruy's designed steady state:
  prepacked cache, bump allocator, cached CPU detection
- constant weight matrices (RuyPrepareB / preloaded parameters) are packed
  once via CachePolicy::kAlwaysCache; shortlist-selected B stays uncached
  (its buffer is reused with changing contents and the prepacked cache
  keys on the data pointer, not the contents)
- staleness guard: TranslationModel teardown bumps a global generation;
  each worker drops its prepacked cache on mismatch before the next GEMM

Host M3 Pro, en-zh, FLORES-150: blocking -6.4%, 4 workers -5.2%, single
sentence -26% (18.6 -> 13.4 ms), RSS flat. Output byte-identical to
vanilla in the deterministic no-shortlist config; with shortlist, within
the engine's pre-existing pass-level divergence envelope.

Untested at runtime: the generation guard's reload path (needs a
load -> unload -> reload case, ideally on device).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
